menu "ULANI status LED"

config ULANI_STATUS_LED_ENABLE
    bool "Enable the status LED"
    default y
    help
        Drives an on-board LED as a status light: off when idle, solid while
        talking to a Tesserae server, and blinking while streaming a frame to
        the calendar over BLE. Turn this off to leave the pin alone.

choice ULANI_BOARD
    prompt "Board preset (sets the LED pin)"
    depends on ULANI_STATUS_LED_ENABLE
    default ULANI_BOARD_C3_SUPERMINI
    help
        ESP-IDF has no built-in board database (unlike Zephyr's devicetree), so
        the LED pin is chosen here. Pick your board for sensible defaults, or
        Custom to set the pin and polarity by hand. Add a new board by adding a
        preset below and giving it defaults on the two options that follow.

config ULANI_BOARD_C3_SUPERMINI
    bool "ESP32-C3 Super Mini (blue LED on GPIO8, active-low)"

config ULANI_BOARD_CUSTOM
    bool "Custom"

endchoice

config ULANI_STATUS_LED_GPIO
    int "Status LED GPIO number"
    depends on ULANI_STATUS_LED_ENABLE
    default 8 if ULANI_BOARD_C3_SUPERMINI
    default 8 if ULANI_BOARD_CUSTOM
    range 0 48
    help
        The GPIO the status LED is wired to.

config ULANI_STATUS_LED_ACTIVE_LOW
    bool "LED is active-low (lit when the pin is driven low)"
    depends on ULANI_STATUS_LED_ENABLE
    default y if ULANI_BOARD_C3_SUPERMINI
    default n if ULANI_BOARD_CUSTOM
    help
        The C3 Super Mini's blue LED lights when GPIO8 is pulled low, so it is
        active-low. Most discrete "wire an LED to a pin" designs are active-high.

endmenu
